the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Changes from upstream (shunt-muse):
- scripts/lib/aika.sh (Portal CLI / AiKA transport) replaced by
  scripts/lib/muse.sh, which runs one headless `muse exec` turn.
- The bulk-reader and code-writer mode instructions now travel in the prompt.
- Hooks block by exiting 2 with the reason on stderr, and allow silently, so
  the same scripts work as Claude Code and Codex PreToolUse hooks.
- check-bash-read accepts a shell command given as an argv array.
- bulk-read numbers each line in the prompt, so cited line numbers are exact.
- Skill and hook text now points at Muse instead of AiKA.

Changes for the OpenCode port (shunt-opencode):
- Claude Code / Codex hook wiring replaced by plugin/index.ts, an OpenCode 1.x
  plugin whose tool.execute.before hook calls the same two bash scripts and
  blocks by throwing the hook's stderr.
- scripts/lib/muse.sh replaced by scripts/lib/opencode.sh delegating to
  scripts/lib/worker.py, which manages a private, isolated `opencode serve`
  worker and calls its HTTP API directly (the CLI --attach path can exit
  before the event stream finishes in 1.18.34).
- Distribution via install.sh (no marketplace manifest in OpenCode 1.x):
  runtime under ~/.local/share/shunt-opencode, skills under
  ~/.config/opencode/skills with ${SHUNT_ROOT} rewritten.
- SHUNT_MUSE_* configuration replaced by the SHUNT_OPENCODE_* variables
  documented in the README.
